      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Boss, I got it.' — Notice the proper name meaning 'chef, boss' paired with the pronoun for 'I'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Вы добавили базилик, да?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You added basil, right?' The first content word means 'you', and 'basil' rounds out the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Чист.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Clear.' You'll hear 'clean' all the time in the show, here connected with 'clean'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Проверили.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Checked.' You'll hear 'checked' all the time in the show, here connected with 'checked'. And Chef Viktor jumps in.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я так и знал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I knew it.' The key word here means 'I', which Chef Viktor combines with 'knew'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Виктор Петрович, ошибочка вышла.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Viktor Petrovich, a mistake happened.' — Notice the proper name meaning 'Viktor' paired with the proper name for 'Petrovich'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Мои люди проверили этого человека.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'My people checked this person.' the speaker puts 'people' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'checked'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Абсолютно чист.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Completely clean.' In Russian, 'completely' leads into 'clean' in a very natural everyday phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А я всегда знал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And I always knew.' The first content word means 'I', and 'knew' rounds out the thought.",
